tly. Oracle and observation: value_matches compares the decoded bytes with the payload the harness built, and the wire-length event shows the encoder emitted all bytes, so the shortening is attributable to the length field rather than to a truncated write; identity is the shared subject field between the prerequisite and the result. Contrary evidence and limits: the shipped configuration's 1000-byte commands never reach the boundary, no replica reader is exercised so the desynchronisation's consequence on the following message is not observed, and whether the client library caps the size it builds was not read. No counterevidence was found that the codec preserves values in this scope.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the value is constructed by the harness; the client's own allocation cap was not read, so the premise that a caller can reach this size rests on the configuration being a parameter\\\",\n   \\\"the shipped configuration uses 1000-byte commands, so the default deployment never reaches the truncation\\\",\n   \\\"no replica reader consumes the shifted stream, so the desync's effect on the following message is unobserved\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-c10.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-c10.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
